# The Content-Security-Policy in netlify.toml pins the inline import map in
# solar-system/index.html by SHA-256 hash. That hash covers the exact bytes of
# the script, line endings included — so if Git checked this file out with
# CRLF on Windows (the default here), the hash would no longer match, the
# browser would refuse to run the import map, and three.js would fail to load
# at all. Forcing LF keeps the deployed bytes identical everywhere.
solar-system/index.html text eol=lf
